  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Interpeace Principles for Inclusive Peace</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Principles for Inclusive Peace aims to develop a new set of Principles and informal norms for the international community that strengthen and better enable conflict-affected communities and countries to develop more inclusive, effective and enduring peace processes through a participatory process.

The objective is to establish the Principles for Inclusive Peace: new international principles, guidance and informal norms to guide best-practise in the establishment, process and implementation of peace processes and to design a mechanism or platform that will monitor the implementation of the principles and provide practical and implementable guidelines to ensure strategic coherence of peace-making and peacebuilding actions in post-conflict settings.</narrative>
  </description>
